 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you doing? Not exactly. A century is 100 miles, and it' good goal no matter your speed. Would you rather do one big day out, or a few shorter rides leading up to it? Roughly six to eight hours, depending on how you ride. Are you comfortable spending that much time on bike? It is. Want to do it in one go, or spread it over a few days and build up your endurance? Great plan. Pick a trail or a track you like, and start there. Set a target speed, but don't push too hard at first. Roughly three or four rides of two hundred to two fifty miles each build the skills and endurance without overdoing it. A few short sprints help too.",
